WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.153
Hedy Lamarr arrived in America in 1937 as a film star.

2
00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:08.674
She left behind a husband who sold arms, a homeland about

3
00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:11.900
to be swallowed by Nazi Germany, and her father's fortune.

4
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.867
In the summer of 1941, a Hollywood film star filed a

5
00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:19.901
patent for a way to keep the enemy from jamming a torpedo.

6
00:00:20.251 --> 00:00:23.014
She signed it with her legal name: Hedy Kiesler Markey.

7
00:00:23.364 --> 00:00:26.151
The trick was to keep changing the radio frequency.

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.555
A transmitter on a ship and a receiver in the torpedo

9
00:00:29.555 --> 00:00:32.841
would hop from frequency to frequency at the same moment,

10
00:00:32.841 --> 00:00:36.299
guided by matching paper rolls like those in a player piano.

11
00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:41.681
Hedy Lamarr became a United States citizen on 10 April 1953, sixteen

12
00:00:41.681 --> 00:00:46.936
years after she arrived, at a ceremony in federal court in Los Angeles.

13
00:00:47.286 --> 00:00:50.049
Read the full story, with every source, on this page.
